      "textEn": "Another thing is that one should attach one’s jiva to the great Sadhu. Since, when there is no one to tell us of our faults, keeping his company will help one to remain happy. Describe one’s own faults to him. And if they are not noticed by oneself, tell him, “Please mercifully tell me all my faults.” Request like this daily, or every eight days, or every fifteen days, but certainly every month. Since, throughout the month some mistakes must have been made. On this, ‘The Merchant’s Balance Sheet’ Vachanamrut (Gadhada I-38) was narrated, “If payment is not made monthly then it accumulates.” (So do not allow faults to accumulate.) God likes it this way.",
